      "blocks": {
        "opening": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "kicker": "",
            "heading": "Remember when you could <em>just go again?</em>",
            "body": "<p>You used to have more in the tank.</p><p>Now you’re fine until about 3pm. Then everything gets heavier.</p><p><strong>Another coffee. A slow afternoon. Nothing left by the time you get home.</strong></p><p>You’re doing most things right. You eat well, you move, you get to bed at a sensible time.</p><p>And you still don’t feel like yourself.</p>",
            "key": ""
          }
        },
        "familiar": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "kicker": "",
            "heading": "Sound <em>familiar?</em>",
            "body": "<p>If you’re over 35, you’ll probably recognise at least a couple of these.</p>",
            "key": ""
          }
        },
        "m1": {
          "type": "need",
          "settings": {
            "short": "",
            "title": "The 3pm crash",
            "dose_label": "Look for",
            "dose": "",
            "body": "<p>Fine all morning. Then mid-afternoon arrives and you’re reaching for a coffee you know you shouldn’t have.</p>",
            "science": "",
            "claim": "",
            "refs": ""
          }
        },
        "m2": {
          "type": "need",
          "settings": {
            "short": "",
            "title": "Brain fog when you need to be sharp",
            "dose_label": "Look for",
            "dose": "",
            "body": "<p>Slow thinking in the one meeting where you need to be 100% there.</p>",
            "science": "",
            "claim": "",
            "refs": ""
          }
        },
        "m3": {
          "type": "need",
          "settings": {
            "short": "",
            "title": "Heavy legs the next day",
            "dose_label": "Look for",
            "dose": "",
            "body": "<p>A walk, a run or a gym session you used to shake off is still in your legs on the stairs two days later.</p>",
            "science": "",
            "claim": "",
            "refs": ""
          }
        },
        "m4": {
          "type": "need",
          "settings": {
            "short": "",
            "title": "Nothing left for the evening",
            "dose_label": "Look for",
            "dose": "",
            "body": "<p>You get through work. Then there’s nothing in the tank for the people at home, and you can’t just lie on the sofa.</p>",
            "science": "",
            "claim": "",
            "refs": ""
          }
        },
        "m5": {
          "type": "need",
          "settings": {
            "short": "",
            "title": "Waking up groggy",
            "dose_label": "Look for",
            "dose": "",
            "body": "<p>A full night in bed, and you still don’t feel ready for the day.</p>",
            "science": "",
            "claim": "",
            "refs": ""
          }
        },
        "why": {
          "type": "dark",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Why it happens",
            "heading": "It’s not in your head. Your body has changed.",
            "text": "<p>From your mid-30s, your body gets less efficient at turning food into energy. Scientists have measured it: between your late 30s and late 60s, your muscles’ capacity to make energy roughly halves.</p><p>That’s biology. It isn’t willpower, and it isn’t laziness.</p>",
            "step_1_title": "",
            "step_1_text": "",
            "step_2_title": "",
            "step_2_text": "",
            "step_3_title": "",
            "step_3_text": "",
            "end": "And another coffee doesn’t fix it. Caffeine only hides the tiredness. It comes back when the coffee wears off.",
            "refs": "Conley KE, Jubrias SA, Esselman PC. Oxidative capacity and ageing in human muscle. J Physiol. 2000."
          }
        },
        "life": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "kicker": "",
            "heading": "You can’t just <em>take a week off</em>",
            "body": "<p>Life doesn’t stop while you sort it out. Work. Kids. Travel. People who rely on you.</p><p>And not everybody is a 25-year-old PT who can build their whole life around a perfect routine.</p><p><strong>You need something that fits the life you actually have.</strong></p>",
            "key": ""
          }
        },
