        "inside": {
          "type": "answer",
          "settings": {
            "label": "",
            "heading": "What’s inside, <em>in plain English</em>",
            "text": "<p>19 ingredients in two capsules. You don’t need to remember the names. Here’s what the main ones do.</p>",
            "image_url": "",
            "image_alt": "",
            "image_position": "",
            "rows": "B vitamins | Help reduce tiredness and fatigue. All eight are in here, in forms your body can use straight away.\nVitamin D | Supports normal muscle function. Most of us in the UK get too little sun from October to March.\nZinc and copper | Help protect your cells from oxidative stress, which is everyday wear and tear inside your cells.\nNR (a form of vitamin B3) | Your body turns it into NAD+, which every cell uses to make energy. You have less NAD+ as you get older.\nCoQ10 | Part of how your cells make energy. Your body makes less of it after your twenties.\nCreatine (free) | For short bursts of hard effort, like the stairs or a sprint. It comes as a separate pouch, free with your first subscription order.",
            "ticks": "",
            "cta": "See today’s Black Friday offer",
            "cta_link": "",
            "foot": "Vitamins B2, B3, B5, B6, B12 and folate contribute to the reduction of tiredness and fatigue. Vitamin D contributes to the maintenance of normal muscle function. Zinc and copper contribute to the protection of cells from oxidative stress. Creatine increases physical performance in successive bursts of short-term, high-intensity exercise; the beneficial effect is obtained with a daily intake of 3g of creatine. Food supplements are not a substitute for a varied, balanced diet and a healthy lifestyle. If your tiredness is new, severe or doesn’t lift, speak to your GP. If you take medication, or are pregnant or breastfeeding, check with your doctor before taking supplements."
          }
        },
        "timeline": {
          "type": "timeline",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What to expect, <em>week by week</em>",
            "sub": "What customers tell us they notice. Individual results vary.",
            "intro": "It’s a long burn, not a quadruple espresso. Score how your afternoons feel out of 10 on day 1, then compare.",
            "items": "Day 1: Your starting point | Two capsules with breakfast. CoQ10 and vitamins D3 and K2 dissolve in fat, so food helps your body take them in.\nDays 3–7: More energy, within days | The first thing most people tell us they notice: less of the 3pm wall, and energy left for the evening. B vitamins contribute to the reduction of tiredness and fatigue.\nDay 30: Afternoons that hold | The lift stops being a good day and becomes your normal. Compare your afternoon score with day 1.\nDay 60: Ready to go again | A walk, a round of golf or a gym session stops hanging around for days. Vitamin D contributes to normal muscle function.\nDay 90: Feeling like yourself | Many people say they hadn’t realised how flat they’d been. Not for you? Every subscription payment back, less delivery.",
            "foot": "What customers tell us, not a clinical study, and not a guaranteed outcome. Our first UK clinical trial starts this December."
          }
        },
